(7166030, 1100268, 114285, '<td valign="top">Incredibly frustrating but true, sad what hope do they have :(<br/> <br/>Whatever happened to a good book!<br/> <br/>Thanks for documenting true life.</td>', 'Incredibly frustrating but true, sad what hope do they have :( Whatever happened to a good book! Thanks for documenting true life.', '2014-01-31 01:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7166041, 1100338, 143098, '<td valign="top">Nice pastoral feel to it.</td>', 'Nice pastoral feel to it.', '2014-01-31 01:18:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7166057, 1099805, 69450, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, but I think it would be really strong if you cropped in the sides so the centre of the arch was at the centre of the image, cropped the bottom so it was just past the power pole reflections, cropped the top so the top of the bridge was on a 1/3 line, and then cloned out the power poles and lines in the sky and pole reflections in the water. (Though the cropping alone would be a big improvement)</td>', 'Nice shot, but I think it would be really strong if you cropped in the sides so the centre of the arch was at the centre of the image, cropped the bottom so it was just past the power pole reflections, cropped the top so the top of the bridge was on a 1/3 line, and then cloned out the power poles and lines in the sky and pole reflections in the water. (Though the cropping alone would be a big improvement)', '2014-01-31 01:55:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7166083, 1099891, 58667, '<td valign="top">Just passing through at the moment. This is very beautiful. Just when sharpening, use a layer mask to not sharpen the bokeh. I can also see the halo of sharpening, especially on the foot. I believe this can be avoided to an extent by using a smaller radius (say 0.3 or 0.4) and then increasing the amount (assuming you used USM). This looks like it was already sharp, so the oversharpening was probably not that necessary. But a stunning photo and excellent colours! I really like it!</td>', 'Just passing through at the moment. This is very beautiful. Just when sharpening, use a layer mask to not sharpen the bokeh. I can also see the halo of sharpening, especially on the foot. I believe this can be avoided to an extent by using a smaller radius (say 0.3 or 0.4) and then increasing the amount (assuming you used USM). This looks like it was already sharp, so the oversharpening was probably not that necessary. But a stunning photo and excellent colours! I really like it!', '2014-01-31 03:48:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7166084, 1100505, 58667, '<td valign="top">lol. Well, it is a nice photo of it. I can see this printed as an almost abstract piece of art next to other pieces (maybe not on its own). The only thing distracting me is the shadow on the top right.</td>', 'lol. Well, it is a nice photo of it. I can see this printed as an almost abstract piece of art next to other pieces (maybe not on its own). The only thing distracting me is the shadow on the top right.', '2014-01-31 03:53:34.000000', NULL, 1),
