(7166627, 1099193, 144365, '<td valign="top">Not a fan of the title. <br/> <br/>I always give one ten in every challenge. This was one of the easiest choices I''ve made in this regard for any challenge. In my opinion, there isn''t another photo that comes close to the impact this one is presenting. I might not give any photo a nine because I believe this one is that much better than the rest.<br/> <br/>It''s one of the only entries where I want to ask follow up questions. I want to engage with the subjects of the photo. You want the photo that proceeds this one to come next.</td>', 'Not a fan of the title.  I always give one ten in every challenge. This was one of the easiest choices I''ve made in this regard for any challenge. In my opinion, there isn''t another photo that comes close to the impact this one is presenting. I might not give any photo a nine because I believe this one is that much better than the rest. It''s one of the only entries where I want to ask follow up questions. I want to engage with the subjects of the photo. You want the photo that proceeds this one to come next.', '2014-01-31 20:20:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7166629, 1100268, 124815, '<td valign="top">Great scene and great shot and good processing.<br/>I can see it painted by one of the British painters, Stanley Spencer or Paula Rego or someone like Balthus<br/>I had the first feel that the composition was better without the lamp but I was so wrong; the lamp adds so much to the domesticity of the scene and to the composition lines.</td>', 'Great scene and great shot and good processing.I can see it painted by one of the British painters, Stanley Spencer or Paula Rego or someone like BalthusI had the first feel that the composition was better without the lamp but I was so wrong; the lamp adds so much to the domesticity of the scene and to the composition lines.', '2014-01-31 20:23:21.000000', NULL, 1),
